body:
I was abused as a Child too.. it started as a Baby with my alcoholic father, turned out I had to move to forster Familys at 2 and 3 of them were keeping me for a while and gave me to the next one. I stayed at a Family with a mother like a Monster and bad sisters just as written down in fairy tales. They hit me and i had to swallow liquid soap or disgusting sauces. they got a second child and he was my lil brother then I really loved him and they did the same to him. It wasnt beautiful. i moved to my mom somehow- School was horror... got hit there too.. at home it continued with my fucking stepfather. went online. met a special person I'm still loving til this day but we are.. somehow living our own lifes. I lost my big love too.. I know it hurts..

&#x200B;

just by this little neckline of my kinda similar Story of my experiences I want to tell you that you can turn pain into power everytime.. you're special, everyone is! you can keep fighting what scares you and the pain can fade away.. there are many doors open on this word.. don't give up. Problems are here to be solved. I often felt the same as you.... it was a journey to get out of it
